            <ArticleTitle>Skin cooling, pain and chronic wound healing progression.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S21, S24-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are many areas of wound care where theory does not always match the practical experiences of the patient. This article discusses the effects of two factors--skin cooling and pain--on chronic wound healing, and the role of pain and inflammation on the overall wound healing process.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
